id: pm-gh1617
title: "GH-1617: make history display order explicit and consistent across projections"
description: "GitHub #1617 reports implicit history direction changes with limit and projection, breaking replay. Add a typed SDK/CLI/MCP order option with documented defaults, preserving latest-window selection, physical indices, diff alignment and continuation."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: agent-ux,github,history,sdk
created_at: "2026-10-28T15:27:06.469Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T16:46:57.489Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T16:40:15.282Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T16:40:15.282Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 100
acceptance_criteria: SDK validates order before history reads;CLI and MCP expose identical ordering;Every projection aligns row and diff order across limits;Document defaults and chronological replay compatibility
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: low
confidence: 95
resolution: "Added oldest_first/newest_first display ordering after latest-N selection, preserving full-history chronological defaults and diff replay. CLI contracts, top-level MCP forwarding, valid schema examples, docs and SDK compatibility snapshot are aligned."
expected_result: "Limits must not silently flip compact/provenance display order, and callers must be able to request chronological replay through every public transport."
actual_result: "48 linked history tests pass, including the projection/limit/order matrix, physical diff coordinates, CLI and nested/top-level runtime requests. The pinned semantic negative control fails the intended ordering assertion. Typecheck and packed Node/Bun continuation pass. Exact-head hosted checks remain required before merge; full local coverage is not claimed."
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
