comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T15:27:06.469Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict 3146-item all-status corpus without omissions, history search and open/in-progress lists found no GH1617 owner. Completed pm-gh1605 remains closed; this is a display-contract follow-up."
  "2026-10-28T15:28:07.749Z","harness:codex","Implementation decision: explicit order applies identically to compact, provenance and full rows plus value diffs. Preserve full/raw chronological default; compact/provenance default newest_first independent of limit. Document both defaults and require --order oldest_first for chronological compact replay. Latest-N selection remains independent of presentation."
  "2026-10-28T15:42:07.989Z","harness:codex","Red/green proof: new persistent history fixture fails on unchanged source with newest_first versus requested oldest_first. Implemented explicit SDK validation and CLI/MCP enum, consistent latest-N presentation, aligned value diffs and documented compatibility. Linked history cohort passes48tests. Complete all-source coverage and static/current-head hosted admission remain pending."
  "2026-10-28T16:25:14.752Z","harness:codex","CodeRabbit review found top-level MCP/runtime order was accepted by schema but not hoisted. Added forwarding and a top-level oldest_first regression alongside nested options coverage; corrected action-specific schema examples. Full local coverage run: 11520 passing, two failures (global npm module resolution and 30-second scale benchmark timeout); no coverage artifact produced, so no full-coverage pass is claimed."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T15:47:48.508Z","harness:codex","Selection and presentation are separate contracts: limit chooses the latest matching entries; order chooses their display direction. Replay the complete authoritative chain before selecting value diffs so excluded updates still establish before-values."
